  "claim_short": "Under the full hypotheses in the source, a closed shift-invariant subspace contains a nonzero polynomial if and only if it has finite codimension. Every such subspace is exactly d P^2(mu) for a polynomial d whose zeros lie in the open disk, and is therefore cyclic. In addition, all invariant subspaces are cyclic whenever the P^2(mu) norm is equivalent to the Hardy norm; this includes every rotationally invariant...",
